The Artem detector uses utterances synthesized through OpenRouter
(https://openrouter.ai/collections/text-to-speech-models/) and with Silero V4
(Silero Team, https://github.com/snakers4/silero-models) and Piper Russian voices
(https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices). Training background audio comes
from MUSAN (David Snyder, Guoguo Chen, and Daniel Povey, CC BY 4.0,
https://www.openslr.org/17/) and FLEURS (Google, CC BY 4.0,
https://huggingface.co/datasets/google/fleurs).
